<title>USA: U.S. Nov durable goods orders fell 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Nov durable goods orders fell 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	Nov     Oct--Rev from     Sept</p>
<p>  New Orders		 -1.6     0.5     0.3	 4.5</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.  Unch    -6.8    -7.7	19.0</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.    -2.2     3.0     2.9	 0.3</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	-3.4     0.4     0.6	 4.5</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders     55.2     2.0    -8.6	 7.1</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders  -7.8    -0.4    Unch	15.4</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   -1.6     1.6     2.2	 2.2</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Nov	Oct---Rev from    Sept</p>
<p> New Orders		171.76   174.64   174.35    173.81</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  41.58    41.60    41.19     44.64</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   130.17   133.04   133.10    129.17</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     163.45   169.28   169.56    168.56</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	8.31     5.36     4.80	5.25</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  43.63    47.34    47.53     47.52</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   37.66    38.28    38.48     37.67</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	Nov     Oct--Rev from     Sept</p>
<p> Total Shipments	    0.8    -1.2    -1.1	 1.3</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders    0.3     1.2     1.1	 0.7</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Nov	Oct---Rev from    Sept</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 170.10   168.70   168.83    170.71</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   488.52   486.87   486.45    480.93</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES   Nov     Oct--Rev from     Sept</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	    0.2    -1.9    -0.6	-3.7</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery    0.3    -1.7    -1.4	-0.2</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery   -9.3    16.9    17.2	 0.2</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  14.37    14.34   14.52     14.62</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  31.86    31.75   31.84     32.30</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  28.23    31.14   31.22     26.64</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected November durable goods orders to rise 0.1 percent. Excluding defense orders, they expected a 0.5 percent drop.</p>
<p>November durables orders excluding transporation had the largest decline since a 2.4 percent drop in January 1993, the department said.</p>
<p>Total durables orders, durables excluding transportation and excluding defense orders marked their first decline since August.</p>
<p>In transportation equipment orders during November, all component industries increased except aircraft and parts.</p>
